BT /F1 10 Tf 50 800 Td 14 TL () ' (ARTICLE 1 DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION) ' (This Facility Agreement is made between Godavari Healthcare Limited \(the Borrower\) and) ' (Bharat Commercial Bank Limited \(the Lender\) for a term loan facility of INR 260 crore.) ' () ' (Business Day means a day on which banks are open for general business in Mumbai. Financial) ' (Year means the period of twelve months ending on 31 March of each year.) ' () ' (EBITDA means profit before tax, interest, depreciation and amortisation, as shown in the) ' (audited consolidated financial statements of the Borrower.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 2 THE FACILITY) ' (The Borrower may request a drawdown by giving the Lender not less than 5 \(five\) Business) ' (Days notice, and each drawdown shall not be less than INR 25 crore.) ' () ' (The Borrower may prepay the facility after giving not less than 30 \(thirty\) days prior) ' (written notice to the Lender.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 6 FINANCIAL COVENANTS) ' (6.1 EBITDA to EMI shall not be less than 1.50 times in any quarter.) ' () ' (6.2 The Current Ratio of the Borrower shall be at least 1.33 times.) ' () ' (6.3 Total Debt to EBITDA shall not be more than 2.75 times.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 7 UNDERTAKINGS) ' (7.1 The Borrower shall maintain proper books of account and records in accordance with) ' (Indian Accounting Standards.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 9 EVENTS OF DEFAULT) ' (Any amount unpaid for more than 7 \(seven\) days after its due date is an Event of Default.) ' () ' (A cure period of 30 \(thirty\) days applies to any breach of the financial covenants that is) ' (capable of remedy.) ' () ' ET
